+| G7 — “nowhere else” | **CONFIRMED** | Other chapters file system designs; only the degree of chemical detail is arguably unusual. |
+| G8 — causal-language attribution | **CONFIRMED** | The sentence fuses p. 241, pp. 273–274, pp. 276–277, and a 2026 claim. |
+| G9a — 70% workshop rate suspect | **REJECTED** | The 2026 Nature paper explicitly reports 70%; a count of visible archival proceedings is not a reliable acceptance denominator. |
+| G9b — Nature wording is misleading | **CONFIRMED** | Nature published the human system report; the generated workshop paper was withdrawn under protocol. |
+| G9c — A-Lab needs the 2026 correction | **CONFIRMED** | The corrected paper supersedes both the numbers and the novelty formulation. |
+| G9d — unmarked counterfactual/absence claims | **CONFIRMED** | The claims listed in finding 10 bypass the claim gate. |
+| G10 — theory/theory-of-theories row is compound | **CONFIRMED** | It joins a partly present human practice to an unbuilt machine hierarchy. |
+| G11 — pp. 276–277 forecast is unscored | **CONFIRMED** | It is contract-relevant and materially different from p. 280. |
+| G12 — prose/ledger mismatch | **CONFIRMED** | The ledger's specificity and severity do not support the prose's verdict. |
+| A1 — AI Scientist had only simulated review | **REJECTED** | Three manuscripts entered real blind human workshop review; one cleared the threshold before protocol-mandated withdrawal. |
+| A2 — p. 243 must be RIGHT ANSWER, WRONG REASON | **REJECTED** | The mechanism is already a separate p. 251 row; merging it into the functional row would make both rows compound. The HIT is still inflated for G1's different reason. |
+| A3 — formal digital computers were a flat MISS | **REJECTED** | Lem forecast an information crisis, not the impossibility of any digital automation; the reviewer invents “dead end for theory formation.” |
+| A4 — move p. 251 RQWA to problem level | **CONFIRMED** | This row grades a live route dilemma, and its present evidence does not pay every quoted clause. |
+| A5 — skeptical reader sees protected grading | **CONFIRMED** | The table is more favorable than the chapter's own argued conclusion. |
+| A6 — GNoME correction calls belong to 2024 | **REJECTED** | The essay's specific duplicate/correction claim is sourced to December 2025; the 2024 critiques concerned related but different novelty/usefulness objections. [C&EN, 16 Dec. 2025](https://cen.acs.org/research-integrity/Duplicate-structures-haunt-crystallography-databases/103/web/2025/12) |
+
+`./verify.sh` currently passes (196 corpus quotes, 78 claim markers, no mismatches), but that does not cure the interpretive, currency, or unmarked-claim failures above.

